<!-- The SAG Mill, fourth pass: the ingot -> dust step GregTech does not do *yet*.
     Section 6e made Ender IO's ten alloys GregTech materials, so `dustDarkSteel`, `dustEnergeticAlloy`
     and the rest resolve to GregTech's dust (`gregtech:meta_item_1:2179` and so on) - which means
     the SAG Mill's `Sagmill: <alloy> Ingot / Block` recipes had quietly become a non-GregTech source
     of the pack's dusts. GregTech's own macerator makes that dust for nine of the ten - Gregicality
     generates the ingot -> dust recipe itself, which the run's de-duplication log confirms with
     merges such as `duplicate recipe merge: macerator 1xgregtech:meta_item_1:10179 ->
     1xgregtech:meta_item_1:2179` - and the one it does not (soularium) is added to the macerator by
     scripts/eio_materials.zs, so switching the mill's copies off strands nothing. The names are in
     sagmill_metals.xml.
     The same pass takes the two remaining GregTech metals whose SAG entries sit in
     sagmill_modded.xml - signalum and lumium (enderium and invar were already switched off by the
     second pass above; signalum and lumium are listing-only here because their ore names are empty
     in this pack, so Ender IO skips them anyway, and they are named for completeness) - plus the two
     lapis recipes in sagmill.xml, whose names carry no "Sagmill: " prefix, which is why the second
     and third passes could not see them. `Lapis Dust` (gemLapis -> dustLapis) and
     `Lapis Block Dust` (blockLapis -> dustLapis) are the same macerator step GregTech already
     performs on the gem and the block.
     Deliberately kept: `Sagmill: GlowStone` - and that one is not a bypass at all, because
     `dustGlowstone` holds vanilla's glowstone dust, not a GregTech material. `Quartz Dust` was kept
     by the same reasoning and that reasoning was wrong; it is switched off in the fifth pass below. -->
