<!-- The SAG Mill, fifth pass: the ones the earlier passes vouched for and should not have.
     The owner asked for another sweep - *"check which Ender IO recipes bypass the GregTech line"* -
     so the audit was made mechanical: `tools/audit-eio-bypass.ps1` walks every recipe in Ender IO's
     XML, resolves each output through the mod's own alias table, and reports the ones whose output is
     (or resolves to) a **GregTech item**, cross-checked against the instance's user file and Ender IO's
     own "Skipping XML recipe" log so that only recipes which actually run are listed.

     These nine were the mill's remaining GregTech-material outputs. The second and third passes kept
     them because the *input* was something GregTech's maps did not appear to accept, but what matters
     is the output: every one of these materials has GregTech producers of its own, checked against the
     full recipe-map dump - aluminium dust 61, coal dust 16, certus quartz dust 16, sulfur dust 21,
     nether quartz dust 17, wheat dust 4, obsidian dust 4, silicon 14 - so switching the mill's copies
     off moves the step to GregTech instead of stranding anything. In particular GregTech's macerator
     *does* take a nether quartz gem, wheat and vanilla obsidian, which is what the third pass's
     reasoning had missed (`macerator IN minecraft:quartz:0`, `IN minecraft:wheat:0`,
     `IN {blockObsidian, obsidian}`). -->
